("For 2000--2019, the best estimate (\\tbc{$-0.202$}\\,m\\,w.e.\\,yr$^{-1}$) is \\tbc{0.014}\\,m\\,w.e.\\,yr$^{-1}$ less negative than the area-weighted value of \\citet{Hugonnet2021} for regions 13--15 ($-0.216 \\pm 0.027$), and the same offset appears in each RGI region (\\tbc{$-0.180$}, \\tbc{$-0.130$} and \\tbc{$-0.453$} against $-0.195$, $-0.137$ and $-0.468$). Every glacier reproduces its own geodetic target, so the offset arises from the aggregation. The model weights each year by the glacier area of that year, which shrinks under volume--area scaling, whereas the geodetic per-glacier rates refer to the fixed RGI area. In mass terms, the modelled 2000--2019 loss is \\tbc{19.0}--\\tbc{19.1}\\,Gt\\,yr$^{-1}$, against 21.1\\,Gt\\,yr$^{-1}$ in \\citet{Hugonnet2021}. \\tbc{[This offset is removed by the area-consistent calibration of run\\_06; to be updated.]}",
 "In mass terms, the four forcings that cover 2000--2019 give a modelled loss of 20.4--20.6\\,Gt\\,yr$^{-1}$ for the glaciers in the regional series, against 21.0--21.1\\,Gt\\,yr$^{-1}$ from the per-glacier rates of \\citet{Hugonnet2021} for the same glaciers, and $21.1 \\pm 3.0$\\,Gt\\,yr$^{-1}$ in their regional estimate for HMA (95\\,\\% confidence interval, regions combined in quadrature; $\\pm5.2$\\,Gt\\,yr$^{-1}$ if the regional errors are summed). The remaining difference of 2.1--2.7\\,\\% is the residual of the area-consistent target (Sect.~\\ref{sec:res_calib}); calibrated to the specific rate without that correction, the model gave 19.0--19.1\\,Gt\\,yr$^{-1}$. "
 "In specific terms, the 2000--2019 best estimate ($-0.219$\\,m\\,w.e.\\,yr$^{-1}$) is 0.003\\,m\\,w.e.\\,yr$^{-1}$ more negative than the area-weighted value of \\citet{Hugonnet2021} for regions 13--15 ($-0.216 \\pm 0.027$), with $-0.197$, $-0.138$ and $-0.493$ against $-0.195$, $-0.137$ and $-0.468$ in regions 13, 14 and 15. The specific value can be slightly more negative while the mass loss is slightly smaller, because the model divides the mass change of each year by the modelled area of that year, which is smaller than the RGI area; the effect is largest in region 15, where the area shrinks most."),
